e initiation of the inflammatory response after postischemic injury.</article-title> <source>Shock</source> <year>2002</year>;<volume>18</volume>:<fpage>169</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12166782</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hierholzer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalff</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Billiar</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Induced nitric oxide promotes intestinal inflammation following hemorrhagic shock.</article-title> <source>Am J Physiol Gastrointest Liver Physiol</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>286</volume>:<fpage>G225</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>33</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14715517</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thillaye-Goldenberg</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Goureau</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Naud</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Delayed onset and decreased severity of experimental autoimmune uveoretinitis in mice lacking nitric oxide synthase type 2.</article-title> <source>J Neuroimmunol</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>110</volume>:<fpage>31</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11024532</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liversidge</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dick</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gordon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Nitric oxide mediates apoptosis through formation of peroxynitrite and Fas/Fas-ligand interactions in experimental autoimmune uveitis.</article-title> <source>Am J Pathol</source> <year>2002</year>;<volume>160</volume>:<fpage>905</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11891189</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rajendram</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Saraswathy</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Photoreceptor mitochondrial oxidative stress in early experimental autoimmune uveoretinitis.</article-title> <source>Br J Ophthalmol</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>91</volume>:<fpage>531</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17035279</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b18"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miyahara</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiryu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyamoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>In vivo three-dimensional evaluation of leukocyte behavior in retinal microcirculation of mice.</article-title> <source>Invest Ophthalmol Vis Sci</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>45</volume>:<fpage>4197</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>201</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15505075</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b19"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>XQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Charles</surname><given-names>IG</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Alterrd immune responses in mice lacking inducible nitric oxide synthase.</article-title> <source>Nature</source> <year>1995</year>;<volume>375</volume>:<fpage>408</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7539113</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hickey</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharkey</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Sihota</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Inducible nitric oxide synthase-deficient mice have enhanced leukocyte-endothelium interactions in endotoxemia.</article-title> <source>Faseb J</source> <year>1997</year>;<volume>11</volume>:<fpage>955</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9337148</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sennlaub</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Courtois</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Goureau</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Inducible nitric oxide synthase mediates retinal apoptosis in ischemic proliferative retinopathy.</article-title> <source>J Neurosci</source> <year>2002</year>;<volume>22</volume>:<fpage>3987</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12019318</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b22"><label>22</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dal Secco</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Moreira</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Freitas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Nitric oxide inhibits neutrophil migration by a mechanism dependent on ICAM-1: role of soluble guanylate cyclase.</article-title> <source>Nitric Oxide</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>15</volume>:<fpage>77</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>86</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16621629</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b23"><label>23</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Charlotte</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ito</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Highly selective inhibitor of inducible nitric oxide synthase enhances S-antigen-induced uveitis.</article-title> <source>Curr Eye Res</source> <year>2003</year>;<volume>26</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12789530</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b24"><label>24</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rosenbaum</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Brischetto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Crespo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Simultaneous in vivo imaging of leukocyte migration: heterogeneity among iris, limbus, and choroid vessels.</article-title> <source>Curr Eye Res</source> <year>2002</year>;<volume>24</volume>:<fpage>214</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12221530</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b25"><label>25</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>O&#x02019;Rourke</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Blackman</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Reduced leukocyte migration, but normal rolling and arrest, in interleukin-8 receptor homologue knockout mice.</article-title> <source>Invest Ophthalmol Vis Sci</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>41</volume>:<fpage>1812</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10845602</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b26"><label>26</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miyamoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogura</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamada</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>In vivo neutralization of P-selectin inhibits leukocyte-endothelial interactions in retinal microcirculation during ocular inflammation.</article-title> <source>Microvasc Res</source> <year>1998</year>;<volume>55</volume>:<fpage>230</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9657923</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b27"><label>27</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tamura</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiryu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyamoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>In vivo evaluation of ocular inflammatory responses in experimental diabetes.</article-title> <source>Br J Ophthalmol</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>89</volume>:<fpage>1052</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16024864</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>